-- SI7-BLIZZ 29725 SI:7 Report: Fire From the Sky: shrine positions from the client data, "Return to camp" only after all three shrines, scene targets limited to the scene player (dev test 5-11-2026 01:07, Labdwarf).
-- (1) The three shrine triggers 55350/55349/55351 stood on the Wowhead-comment spots (813,-1970 / 813,-1760 / 953,-1830 = lake shore, hozen tents, no shrine). The retail quest POI blobs of 29725 (quest_poi_points: 700,-2033 / 735,-1700 / 997,-1901) coincide with the three "Pa_Shrine_Jadedragon_Large_02" doodads of the Serpent's Heart terrain (vmaps 0972_35_30.vmtile, terrain swap 972 is default on map 870: 698,-2034,72 / 740,-1705,68 / 1000,-1902,71; ground z measured with .gps 72.6 / 69.0 / 68.5 + 2.3 water). The triggers (and Gizmo/Socks next to the SW shrine) move there; the video shows Sully on the stone platform of the northern shrine at 3:57.
-- (2) "After scoutin' the three shrines, I headed back over to camp" (54039) and the camp trigger 55352 came from the northern list alone: a player who scouts the northern shrine first and then walks past the camp ended the scene without the other two credits. Now every shrine list reports Data 10/1 to the Sully vehicle, the vehicle counts (counter 1), and at 3 it speaks 54039/54040 and summons the camp trigger (new list 5528602).
-- (3) Targets: credits, the teleport home and the failsafe used "all players within 45/300 yd"; on a shared world that hits bystanders. Credits and the teleport now go to the closest player (the passenger stands on the trigger), the failsafe to the vehicle's summoner (the player cast 103237).
-- (4) The Lurking Tiger (103994, faction 14) attacked the first hostile unit in reach: on dev 01:29:41 it took scene-Rell 55355 (faction 11) at the camp the moment it spawned ("Tryin' ta sneak up on ol' Sully" fired, no tiger ever reached the player). On summon it now starts on the closest player (the vehicle rider), as the retail ambush does in the video (1:32, 3:24).
-- (5) The shrine is a 3.5x-scaled model with a pool (the player stands on its walkway/balustrade, .gps 640,-2012 z75 and 664,-2000 z79): trigger radius 25 -> 35 yd.
-- (6) AIName 55286 SmartAI -> SmartVehicleAI: with plain SmartAI the player-driven vehicle runs UpdateVictim/AttackStart/MoveChase/EnterEvadeMode (SmartAI.cpp:387-394, 675-684, 467-503) as soon as the tiger engages it; on dev 01:45:44 the server stopped accepting the rider's movement (vehicle frozen at 700,-2088 while the client walked on). SmartVehicleAI (SmartAI.cpp:982, VehicleAIBase) keeps the SmartAI events/lists but never fights or evades by itself, and dismisses the vehicle after the rider leaves.
-- (8b) The vehicle rows repeat every second (no NOT_REPEATABLE): a one-shot row fired on the tick the trigger appeared, before the trigger's SmartAI was initialised, and was used up (dev 02:37: SW list never started while SE/N ran); the trigger's own Data event is the once-gate.
-- (8) The triggers checked "Sully vehicle 55286 within 35 yd" with SMART_EVENT_DISTANCE_CREATURE, which uses GetCreatureListWithEntryInGrid (grid objects only, SmartScript.cpp:3570); a player-controlled vehicle is a world object and is never found (dev 02:02: trigger at 698,-2034 alive, rider 32 yd away, no credit). The distance check now runs on the vehicle (its target is the grid-object trigger) and sends Data 1/1 to that trigger, which then runs its list.
-- (7) The tiger is summoned beside the vehicle by SAI (55550, timed-or-corpse 180 s) instead of 103994 (random spot up to 60 yd: in Shadybranch Pocket it landed behind the rim with no path to the rider). On a new vehicle, leftovers of an aborted run (triggers, raccoons, hozen) get Data 9 first.
-- Source: quest_poi_points 29725 (client data), vmaps 0972_35_30.vmtile doodad spawns (Pa_Shrine_Jadedragon_Large_02), maps 0972_30_35.map height grid + .gps on dev (ground/liquid z, the ramp out of Shadybranch Pocket at 645,-2052 -> 640,-2012), video https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NRy7i1oxgfg (1:16-1:28 corridor uphill out of the camp, 1:32 tiger on the path, 2:33 SW shrine + Gizmo, 3:57 N shrine platform, 4:17 "after scouting the three shrines"), SmartScript.cpp (StoreCounter -> SMART_EVENT_COUNTER_SET, SMART_TARGET_OWNER_OR_SUMMONER).
-- DERIVED (no sniff): trigger radius 35 yd, Gizmo/Socks 3-6 yd beside the shrine, the counter mechanism itself (retail uses a spell/phase check we do not have), the tiger's attack-on-summon.
-- (9) event_flags 512 ("WHILE_CHARMED" in the earlier files) is SMART_EVENT_FLAG_DIFFICULTY_RAID40 on this core (SmartScriptMgr.h:1428): such rows never run on map 870; the vehicle rows of 55286 now carry flags 0/1. There is no charm check in SmartScript::ProcessEvent here, so vehicle events fire while the player drives.
